    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="0755" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/9–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Minister to Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-18T17:00:00+03:06">September 18,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>282. ReDepts 177, September 12, 5 p.m. Today British colleague<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d812-f1"/> and I jointly notified King of 10,000–ton increase in
                    1944 grain subsidy supply.</p>
                <p>British colleague also has instructions to notify King of (1) extra food supply
                    for 1944 pilgrimage as listed in Legation’s 270, Sept. 8, 2 p.m. and (2) offer
                    to stock food reserves at Jidda under conditions stated in Legation’s 274,
                    September 10, noon. Request similar instructions.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d812-f2"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Repeated Cairo for AEMME.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d812-f1" n="61" xml:id="d812-f1-content">
                <p>Robert B. Ellison, British Chargé.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d812-f2" n="62" xml:id="d812-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 200, September 30, 7 p.m., the Minister was informed as follows: “You
                    are authorized jointly with your British colleague to notify King Ibn Saud of
                    authorization for additional food supplies for the pilgrimage in 1944, as
                    described in your 270, September 8, 2 p.m.” (890F.24/9–1844)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
